  "note": "\"In the case of Tandragee Council, all the members retain office for three years and go out simultaneously.\" Polling began on Monday morning (16 January 1905) in the Courthouse under S. Sterling, town clerk and returning officer; W. H. Atkinson, legal assessor; S. Whiteside, presiding officer. Eleven names on the ballot paper; the result was announced shortly after nine. \"The first nine were duly declared elected, seven of whom were members of the former Council.\" No party labels are printed."
